    "description": "Duquesne Light is the regulated electric transmission and distribution utility serving the Pittsburgh region. Company materials state that it serves approximately 605,000 customers in Allegheny and Beaver counties across an approximately 817-square-mile service territory. The operating model is fully utility-based, with earnings supported by regulated network investment rather than merchant power generation. Public disclosures emphasize a dense urban and suburban footprint and ongoing grid modernization and clean-energy transition work within southwestern Pennsylvania. Duquesne's current shareholder group is publicly identified on its investor site, with GIC as the largest owner and Three Rivers Utility Holdings, the Manulife and PGGM vehicle, holding a 30.4% interest; Manulife's infrastructure team links the investment to Fund I. The current consortium structure reflects ownership changes following the 2007 take-private and later secondary transfers in 2011, 2016, and 2017.",
